course: dictionary
lesson: 14416
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. Overloaded is a good example. «The truck was overloaded with bricks, and it groaned up the hill.» The clues are truck and bricks, so overloaded means carrying more weight than is safe.
explain: «Do not plug so many lamps into one socket, or it will be overloaded.» Now the clues are socket and plug, so overloaded means too much electricity is going through it. Check by swapping in your meaning: «it will have too much electricity going through it» still makes sense.
explain: «Mia had homework, music practice and football all in one day, and she felt overloaded.» Here the clue is felt, so overloaded means having too much to do or think about. Always ask: what does this word mean in this sentence?
fact: Overloaded is the past form of the verb overload, so «overload» and «overloaded» are linked.
fact: «Overloaded» can mean carrying more weight or things than is safe.
fact: An overloaded circuit or socket has too much electricity going through it.
fact: An overloaded person has too much to do or think about.
fact: The same word can have different meanings, so look at the clues around it.
exercise: «The little boat sank because it was overloaded with families and bags.» What does overloaded mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Ready to sail away | Very quiet and calm | *Carrying more weight than is safe
exercise: «Too many devices on one plug can overload the socket.» What does overload mean here? | The plug is brand new | The socket is empty and switched off | The socket is painted red | *Too much electricity going through it
exercise: Sam says, «I am overloaded with work this week.» What does overloaded mean? | Having a full plate of lunch | Having lots of sunshine | Having too little to do | *Having too much to do
test: «The shelf snapped because it was overloaded with heavy books.» What does overloaded mean? | Full of warm light | *Carrying more weight than is safe | Very clean and tidy | Brand new and shiny
test: The fuse blew because the circuit was overloaded. What does overloaded mean here? | Painted with a lovely pattern | Switched off for the night | Full of warm water | *Too much electricity going through it
exam: «After the long week, Ravi felt overloaded and could not think straight.» What does overloaded mean in this sentence? | Hungry after a long walk | *Having too much to do or think about | Carrying a bag that was too heavy | Glowing in the dark
